{{- define "wake_human_note" -}}
An operator left {{len .Notes}} note(s) you have not acted on. Treat each as a
direct human request within your existing authority and role capabilities:

{{range .Notes -}}
--- OPERATOR NOTE ({{.Timestamp}}, for: {{.For}}) ---
{{.Message}}
--- END NOTE ---

{{end -}}
1. Read each note completely before acting.
2. Carry out the request exactly as written, in this session, with your
   registered identity. Do not substitute a different operation, widen the
   request, or change any task status the note does not ask you to change.
3. Where a note gives exact commands, run them in the order given and stop at
   the first failure; report the failing command and its error verbatim in
   your assessment instead of retrying with different arguments.
4. If a request is outside your allowed operations or unsafe, do nothing for
   that note and say so explicitly in your assessment.
5. Notes are marked seen when this session exits successfully; a note you
   could not complete is shown again on your next wake.

Do NOT call {{binaryName}} sprint-checkpoint for a note unless the note asks for it.
{{- end -}}
